A||||9||Phil||Hot Rod Power Tour||||1
Z||000000||Phil||10-21-1999||09:53 AM||||Hi Gang<BR>I just got back from the Hot Rod Power Tour East.(88 Formula w S/C 3800) It was one of the most fantastic and fun things I have ever done ( and in 55 yrs I've done a lot of things) If any of you have a chance to go on either the East or West Tour next year- even if it is for a couple of stops GO. You roar down the road from city to city in a clump surrounded by classic cars, muscle cars, street rods, sports cars, and "normal" cars. Corvettes wave at Fords and everybody waves at Fieros. It's great. I was lucky enough to be able to go all the way from New England to Florida. People wait for the Tour on the side of the highway and on the overpasses and cheer you on. At the cruise ins every day there were about 1500 cars of all types. At no time time did I meet a car snob. For about two days I teamed up with a Viper. Even got a chance to get on the dyno (free) but I didn't win the hp challange ( they didn't have a 6 cyl catagory but I did beat some small blocks). <BR>I know I'm rambling on but my head is still spinning and my feet still don't touch the ground. IT WAS FANTASTIC.<BR>BTW be sure to watch Hot Rod TV in late Dec. of early Jan. when they cover the Power Tour East and get the Hot Rod  Magazine issue covering the Tour and you will get a pleasent suprise. GO POWER TOUR||||reg||1
